c74d480383126ed520172cea18a50cba1239cdc7337af5ed0e7a425\",\"quote\":\"(4) Nothing in this section prevents employers from considering employment prior to a continuous break in service of more than seven years when determining whether an employee has met the 12-month employment requirement. However, if an employer chooses to recognize such prior employment, the employer must do so uniformly, with respect to all employees with similar breaks in service.\",\"start\":2419}],\"id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:092e061567976bda3852718e856bdb54f8e229c70456194d726138c3eb88b432\",\"jurisdiction\":\"\",\"jurisdiction_quote\":\"\",\"kind\":\"permission\",\"logic_text\":\"\",\"meaning_assertion_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:70ac404784da8cb70538e18e6bdaeecf8904e4e9130758aa8ca393cae54e7e24\",\"modality\":\"may\",\"modality_quote\":\"Nothing in this section prevents employers from\",\"object\":\"\",\"occurrence_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:occurrence:5777e757be795f88f9ad54730ff39dcf9b450d3a0a2a821047f63cd586c8e575\",\"origin\":\"aiSuggested\",\"quote\":\"(4) Nothing in this section prevents employers from considering employment prior to a continuous break in service of more than seven years when determining whether an employee has met the 12-month employment requirement. However, if an employer chooses to recognize such prior employment, the employer must do so uniformly, with respect to all employees with similar breaks in service.\",\"references\":[],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:8faa43a24aafd0ba305c5f8163d254488bccfc911519e2d79f29423f2b82e853\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"(4) Nothing in this section prevents employers from considering employment prior to a continuous break in service of more than seven years when determining whether an employee has met the 12-month employment requirement. However, if an employer chooses to recognize such prior employment, the employer must do so uniformly, with respect to all employees with similar breaks in service.\"],\"scope_text\":\"When determining whether an employee has met the 12-month employment requirement.\",\"section_id\":\"section-1\",\"start\":2419,\"summary\":\"Nothing in this section prevents employers from considering employment prior to a continuous break in service of more than seven years when determining whether an employee has met the 12-month employment requirement.\",\"target_ids\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
